emission tomography</article-title><source>Laryngoscope</source><year>1999</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>970</fpage><lpage>975</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005537-199906000-00024</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Farber LA, Benard F, Machtay M, Smith RJ, Weber RS, Weinstein GS, Chalian AA, Alavi A, Rosenthal DI (1999) Detection of recurrent head and neck squamous cell carcinomas after radiation therapy with 2-18F-fluoro-2-deoxy-d-glucose positron emission tomography. Laryngoscope 109:970&#x02013;975. doi:10.1097/00005537-199906000-00024 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10369292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greven</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>DW</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name><name><surname>Keyes</surname><given-names>JW</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>McGuirt</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>NE</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Case</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Can positron emission tomography distinguish tumor recurrence from irradiation sequelae in patients treated for larynx cancer?</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>353</fpage><lpage>357</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Greven KM, Williams DWIII, Keyes JW Jr, McGuirt FW, Watson NE Jr, Case LD (1997) Can positron emission tomography distinguish tumor recurrence from irradiation sequelae in patients treated for larynx cancer? Cancer 3:353&#x02013;357 </citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greven</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname